law.text:
		Every applicant for a license to catch or take fish shall pay the following license fee or such fee as it may be subsequently revised by the Commission pursuant to § 28.2-201:

On each pound net, $25;


On each stake gill net of 1,200 feet in length or under with a fixed location, $15;


On all other gill nets up to 600 feet, $10;


On all other gill nets over 600 feet and up to 1,200 feet, $15;


On each person using a cast net or throw net or similar device, $8;


On each fyke net head, weir, or similar device, $8;


For up to 100 fish pots or eel pots, $12;


For over 100 but not more than 300 fish pots or eel pots, $20;


For over 300 fish pots or eel pots, $50;


For fish trotlines, $12;


On each person using or operating a fish dip net, $6;


On each haul seine under 500 yards in length used for catching fish, $29; or


On each haul seine from 500 yards up to 1,000 yards in length used for catching fish, $88.
